PS Vita in-app self-update (app/src/utils/vita_install.cpp, issue #14)
  The technique used to install a homebrew VPK from within the app — forging a
  self-signed fake-package "head.bin" and promoting the extracted directory with
  ScePromoterUtility — is the de-facto interoperability standard shared by every
  PS Vita homebrew installer, originating from the HENkaku / molecularShell
  lineage. The canonical reference implementation is VitaShell by TheOfficialFloW
  (https://github.com/TheOfficialFloW/VitaShell), licensed under the GNU General
  Public License v3.0.

  The C++ in vita_install.cpp is an independent reimplementation. The fake-package
  header template embedded in app/src/utils/vita_head_bin.h is copied verbatim
  from VitaShell's resources/head.bin (a fixed functional artifact the patched
  system promoter requires; sha256
  cbb88299319048e19115a1fc9c76b04e33745291749de0e08963b9b425623f45).

  The PS Vita build links a GPL build of libmpv, so the distributed pleNx.vpk is
  already a GPL combined work; reusing this GPLv3-derived material in that binary
  is licence-compatible. This attribution is provided in recognition of that
  origin.
